=== Dot product
The dot product of vectors $bold(u)$ and $bold(v)$ in $n$ dimensions is given by:
$
    chevron.l bold(u), bold(v) chevron.r = u_1 dot v_1 + u_2 dot v_2 + ... + u_n dot v_n
$

=== Magnitude

The magnitude of a vector $bold(v)$ in $n$ dimensions is given by:
$
    |bold(v)| = sqrt(v_1^2 + v_2^2 + ... + v_n^2)
$

The dot product of two Euclidean vectors $bold(u)$ and $bold(v)$ is defined by

$
    chevron.l bold(u), bold(v) chevron.r = |bold(u)| dot |bold(v)| dot cos(theta)
$

